# Keep build artifacts out of the build context.
#
# ecdl-sink is a compiled binary produced by a local `go build`. It is host-arch
# and it is 10 MB. Sending it to the builder causes two problems: it makes up most of the
# context upload for a multi-arch build that recompiles from source anyway, and a
# stray COPY . . would copy a stale amd64 binary into an arm64 image, which then
# fails at runtime with an exec format error that does not indicate the cause.
ecdl-sink
*.test
*.out

# Local module cache, if anyone has vendored or built in place.
vendor/
